---
import PublicationLayout from '../../layouts/PublicationLayout.astro';
import { PUBLICATIONS } from '../../data/publications';
import { R5_DISCUSSION } from '../../data/site-facts';

const publication = PUBLICATIONS.find((item) => item.href === R5_DISCUSSION.articleUrl)!;
---

<PublicationLayout
  category={publication.category}
  type={publication.type}
  title={publication.title}
  description={publication.summary}
  published={publication.date}
  updated={publication.updated}
  status={publication.status}
  toc={[]}
>
  <section id="discussion">
    <h2>A proposal for inspectable evidence across design families</h2>
    <p>
      Public discussion opened on September 17, 2026 for a nomue Protocol Release 5
      proposal covering cross-family declared-design evidence. The proposal asks how
      different design families can expose compatible evidence without making the
      Protocol responsible for product-side method selection.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is an informative proposal open for comment. It issues no identifier,
      schema, check, bundle, supported capability, or adoption. <a
        href={R5_DISCUSSION.proposalUrl}>Read the fixed candidate</a> or <a
        href={R5_DISCUSSION.issueUrl}>join the public discussion</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="proposal">
    <h2>Four proposed additions</h2>
    <p>
      Release 5 proposes versioned per-Profile projection mappings, a selection-timing
      status, an explicit successor non-claim boundary, and a common inspectable
      verification-report view. The projection would consume existing family-owned
      identities and admissibility results rather than creating duplicate authority.
    </p>
    <p>
      The first slice considers independent two-group, paired two-condition, and
      independent multi-group designs. Each family remains conditional on a separately
      accepted Contract and bundle. The proposal does not standardize a product’s
      selection policy or claim that a selected tuple is optimal, fair, scientifically
      true, or numerically correct.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="boundary">
    <h2>What remains open</h2>
    <p>
      The opening record retains holds for independent methodological review, family
      Contract/Profile/schema/bundle acceptance, exact mappings and report encoding,
      historical-preservation fixtures, and the final impact assessment. Public
      discussion is reversible preparation, not a normative design freeze.
    </p>
    <p>
      The minimum discussion period is 30 calendar days under the provisional
      STABLE-INTENT assessment. It began at <time datetime={R5_DISCUSSION.openedAt}>00:38:15 UTC on September 17, 2026</time>;
      the earliest decision is <time datetime={R5_DISCUSSION.earliestDecisionAt}>00:38:15 UTC on October 17, 2026</time>.
      Elapsed time does not imply adoption or a product release.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="participate">
    <h2>How to take part</h2>
    <p>
      Comment on <a href={R5_DISCUSSION.issueUrl}>the public discussion issue</a> with
      the clause or example concerned, an interoperability or methodological issue,
      and a proposed correction or counterexample where possible. The proposal
      particularly welcomes scrutiny of projection ownership, timing conventions,
      non-claims, and conditional family dependencies.
    </p>
    <p><a href={R5_DISCUSSION.openingRecordUrl}>Read the opening record</a>.</p>
  </section>
</PublicationLayout>
